{"path":"/Deep Research App/start","args":{"user_query":"Research-and-build assignment: Create "OpenHands Learning Environment" centered on https://openhands.dev, as a genuinely working, touch-first interactive learning website, optimized for iPad Pro M2 portrait/landscape and responsive on phones/desktops. The user's complete detailed assignment appears in the conversation and is authoritative. Research FIRST, grounded in official current documentation, repositories, releases/tags/commits, maintainer discussions, licensing and version boundaries. Research date: 2026-10-09. Do not conflate legacy OpenHands architecture with current components, hosted offerings, or self-hosted deployments. Investigate task-to-result mechanism, agent/model/provider/tool/runner/workspace boundaries, permissions/secrets, observability, state, persistence, recovery, VM resource/network dependencies, upgrades/rollback, extension routes. Distinguish documented, source-established, tested, inferred, unresolved. Use Exa for primary source discovery and Context7 for release-matched documentation where available. Cite technical claims closely, include links, version tags, limitations and unresolved questions. Unknown learner VM OS/RAM/storage/deployment/OpenHands version/model arrangement/modifications must remain explicit nonsecret inputs; no invented values.

Primary deliverable if Sites tools exist in the research/build stage: build, preview, verify and deliver a real accessible website link using Sites; do not mistake a chat visualization for a site feature. Include fully populated Start Here, Explore the System interactive component map and task stepper, Operate OpenHands lessons, Understand the VM with editable Unknown-capable installation profile and evidence-based conditional guidance, Practice and Recover branching simulations with hints/reset, embedded Teach-back with transparent self-check rubric, Adaptation Workbench with generic behavior worksheet/decision guidance, searchable Sources & Reference. Use plain language for technical adults new to programming. Every practical lesson needs purpose, prerequisites, applicable version, starting condition, explanation, action, observable success, failure signs, recovery, evidence, teach-back. Touch-friendly 44px+ targets, keyboard focus, no hover-only interactions, reduced motion, no autoplay, clear simulation labels, mobile portrait accessible list alternative to diagrams, locally persisted notes/attempts/progress/last point/profile/drafts, human-readable export/import, deliberate data clearing, honest scope of persistence and no credentials. Neutral brand; fictional examples unrelated to learner's identity/organization/industry/projects. The first screen must start a substantive activity. Verify navigation, selections, branching, hints/reset, rubric, workbench, sources, state preservation, import/export, responsive portrait/landscape, keyboard/touch, phone/desktop, long notes, invalid/empty states, safe unsaved work, external links. Do not claim any tests not run or any real OpenHands connection.

IMPORTANT environment capability observation: In the present initiating tool environment, Exa and Context7 connectors are present, but there is no tool named Sites or Work Visualize; a separate AppDeploy connector exists but is not Sites. Follow the user's explicit fallback: IF Sites is unavailable in the research environment, deliver a COMPREHENSIVE source-backed Markdown BUILD HANDOFF for a subsequent Sites-enabled stage, not a purported completed website. The handoff must preserve verified lesson scripts/content, architecture and component descriptions, exact source records/URLs, release boundaries, diagram and stepper state specifications, scenarios with correct/incorrect feedback and recovery, VM profile rules, adaptation examples/worksheet, accessibility/persistence requirements, acceptance criteria and tests, ready for Sites to implement without the learner assembling it. Explicitly label handoff, site not built or deployed. Do not turn the assignment into a plugin merely because Plugin Autopilot was mentioned; that tool targets plugin packaging, not site creation."}}
